{"task_id": "Mbpp/74", "solution": "def is_samepatterns(sequence: list[str], patterns: list[str]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a given sequence of strings follows the structural pattern defined by another list of strings.\n    A bijective mapping must exist between unique elements in the pattern and unique elements in the sequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(sequence) != len(patterns):\n        return False\n\n    pattern_to_word_map = {}\n    word_to_pattern_map = {}\n\n    for i in range(len(sequence)):\n        word = sequence[i]\n        pattern_char = patterns[i]\n\n        # Check pattern_to_word_map consistency\n        if pattern_char in pattern_to_word_map:\n            if pattern_to_word_map[pattern_char] != word:\n                return False\n        else:\n            pattern_to_word_map[pattern_char] = word\n\n        # Check word_to_pattern_map consistency\n        if word in word_to_pattern_map:\n            if word_to_pattern_map[word] != pattern_char:\n                return False\n        else:\n            word_to_pattern_map[word] = pattern_char\n\n    return True"}
