{"task_id": "Mbpp/77", "solution": "def is_Diff(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if a number is divisible by 11 using the alternating sum of digits rule.\n    Returns True if divisible by 11, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    \n    # Handle 0 explicitly as its alternating sum is 0, which is divisible by 11\n    if number == 0:\n        return True\n\n    s = str(abs(number))\n    alternating_sum = 0\n    # Calculate the alternating sum based on position from the right.\n    # The rightmost digit (position 0 from right) is added, the next is subtracted, and so on.\n    for i, digit_char in enumerate(s):\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        # (len(s) - 1 - i) gives the 0-indexed position from the right\n        if (len(s) - 1 - i) % 2 == 0:  # If position from right is even (0, 2, 4...)\n            alternating_sum += digit\n        else:  # If position from right is odd (1, 3, 5...)\n            alternating_sum -= digit\n            \n    return alternating_sum % 11 == 0"}
