{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "def common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds common elements in a list of nested lists.\n    Returns a set containing elements present in all nested lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    common_elements = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    for i in range(1, len(nested_lists)):\n        current_set = set(nested_lists[i])\n        common_elements = common_elements.intersection(current_set)\n        if not common_elements:\n            break\n            \n    return common_elements"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/120", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Union\n\ndef max_product_tuple(data: List[Tuple[Union[int, float], Union[int, float]]]) -> Union[int, float]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the maximum absolute product between numbers in pairs of tuples within a given list.\n    Returns 0 if the input list is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not data:\n        return 0\n\n    max_abs_product = 0\n\n    for num1, num2 in data:\n        product = num1 * num2\n        abs_product = abs(product)\n        if abs_product > max_abs_product:\n            max_abs_product = abs_product\n    \n    return max_abs_product"}
