{"task_id": "Mbpp/223", "solution": "from typing import List, TypeVar\n\nT = TypeVar('T', comparable=True)\n\nNOT_FOUND: int = -1\n\ndef find_first_occurrence(arr: List[T], target: T) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the index of the first occurrence of target in a sorted list arr using binary search.\n    Returns NOT_FOUND if the target is not present.\n    \"\"\"\n    low, high = 0, len(arr) - 1\n    first_occurrence = NOT_FOUND\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n        if arr[mid] == target:\n            first_occurrence = mid\n            high = mid - 1\n        elif arr[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else:\n            high = mid - 1\n    return first_occurrence\n\ndef is_majority(sorted_array: List[T], n: int, element: T) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given element is a majority element in the sorted array.\n    A majority element occurs strictly more than n/2 times.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return False\n\n    first_occurrence_index = find_first_occurrence(sorted_array, element)\n\n    if first_occurrence_index == NOT_FOUND:\n        return False\n\n    # The majority element must appear at least (n // 2) + 1 times.\n    # If the element at first_occurrence_index + (n // 2) is also the same element,\n    # it implies there are at least (n // 2) + 1 occurrences.\n    potential_majority_index = first_occurrence_index + n // 2\n\n    if potential_majority_index < n and sorted_array[potential_majority_index] == element:\n        return True\n    else:\n        return False"}
