{"task_id": "Mbpp/247", "solution": "def lps(s: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of the input string.\n    Uses dynamic programming with O(n^2) time and space complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(s)\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # dp[i][j] stores the length of the longest palindromic subsequence of s[i...j]\n    dp = [[0] * n for _ in range(n)]\n\n    # All single characters are palindromes of length 1\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i][i] = 1\n\n    # Fill the table for lengths from 2 to n\n    for length in range(2, n + 1):\n        for i in range(n - length + 1):\n            j = i + length - 1\n            if s[i] == s[j]:\n                # If characters match, add 2 (for s[i] and s[j])\n                # plus the LPS of the substring s[i+1...j-1]\n                dp[i][j] = 2 + (dp[i + 1][j - 1] if length > 2 else 0)\n            else:\n                # If characters don't match, take the maximum of\n                # LPS excluding s[i] or LPS excluding s[j]\n                dp[i][j] = max(dp[i + 1][j], dp[i][j - 1])\n    \n    return dp[0][n - 1]"}
