{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "from typing import Dict, Tuple\n\ndef get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the number of possible sequences of length n,\n    such that each element is a positive integer and is greater than or equal to\n    twice the previous element but less than or equal to m.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Memoization table: (current_length, last_element) -> count\n    memo: Dict[Tuple[int, int], int] = {}\n\n    def _calculate_sequences_recursive(\n        current_length: int,\n        last_element: int\n    ) -> int:\n        # Base case: If current_length exceeds n, a valid sequence of length n has been formed.\n        if current_length > n:\n            return 1\n\n        # Return memoized result if already computed for this state.\n        if (current_length, last_element) in memo:\n            return memo[(current_length, last_element)]\n\n        count = 0\n        min_next_element = 2 * last_element\n\n        # Iterate through possible values for the current element.\n        # It must be >= twice the previous element and <= m.\n        for next_element in range(min_next_element, m + 1):\n            count += _calculate_sequences_recursive(\n                current_length + 1,  # Move to the next position in the sequence\n                next_element         # Current element becomes the 'last_element' for the next step\n            )\n\n        # Store the computed count in the memoization table.\n        memo[(current_length, last_element)] = count\n        return count\n\n    # If the target sequence length is 1, any number from 1 to m is a valid sequence.\n    if n == 1:\n        return m\n\n    total_count = 0\n    # For sequences of length n > 1, iterate through all possible first elements.\n    # The recursive helper then finds the ways to complete the sequence from the second element onwards.\n    for first_element in range(1, m + 1):\n        total_count += _calculate_sequences_recursive(\n            current_length=2,       # We are now looking to fill the second position in the sequence\n            last_element=first_element # The chosen first_element is the 'last_element' for this call\n        )\n\n    return total_count"}
