{"task_id": "Mbpp/299", "solution": "import collections\n\ndef max_aggregate(data):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum aggregate score from a list of (name, score) tuples.\n    Returns the name and total score of the individual with the highest aggregate.\n    \"\"\"\n    aggregated_scores = collections.defaultdict(int)\n    for name, score in data:\n        aggregated_scores[name] += score\n\n    if not aggregated_scores:\n        return \"\", 0\n\n    max_name = \"\"\n    max_score = -float('inf')\n\n    for name, score in aggregated_scores.items():\n        if score > max_score:\n            max_score = score\n            max_name = name\n            \n    return max_name, max_score"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/301", "solution": "def dict_depth(data: dict) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum nesting depth of a dictionary.\n    Raises TypeError if input is not a dictionary.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(data, dict):\n        raise TypeError(\"Input must be a dictionary.\")\n\n    if not data:\n        return 1\n\n    max_depth = 1\n    for key, value in data.items():\n        if isinstance(value, dict):\n            max_depth = max(max_depth, 1 + dict_depth(value))\n    return max_depth"}
