{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "def start_withp(word_list: list[str]) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds up to two words starting with 'p' (case-insensitive) from a list of strings.\n    Returns a tuple of the found words, padded with None if fewer than two are found.\n    \"\"\"\n    found_words = []\n    for text in word_list:\n        # Split the string into words based on whitespace\n        words_in_text = text.split()\n        for word in words_in_text:\n            # Check if the word starts with 'p' or 'P'\n            if word and word[0].lower() == 'p':\n                found_words.append(word)\n                if len(found_words) == 2:\n                    return (found_words[0], found_words[1])\n\n    # If fewer than two words were found\n    if len(found_words) == 1:\n        return (found_words[0], None)\n    else:  # 0 words found\n        return (None, None)"}
