{"task_id": "Mbpp/286", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum_repeated(arr: list[int], k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the largest sum of a contiguous array in the modified array\n    formed by repeating the given array k times.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _find_max_subarray_sum(current_arr: list[int]) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Applies Kadane's algorithm to find the maximum sum of a contiguous subarray.\"\"\"\n        if not current_arr:\n            return 0\n\n        max_so_far = current_arr[0]\n        current_max = current_arr[0]\n\n        for i in range(1, len(current_arr)):\n            current_max = max(current_arr[i], current_max + current_arr[i])\n            max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n        \n        return max_so_far\n\n    if not arr or k == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    max_sum_single_arr = _find_max_subarray_sum(arr)\n\n    if k == 1:\n        return max_sum_single_arr\n\n    total_sum_arr = sum(arr)\n\n    # For k > 1\n    if total_sum_arr > 0:\n        # If total sum is positive, repeating the array multiple times\n        # will increase the sum. We need to consider the max sum\n        # from two concatenations, and add (k-2) * total_sum_arr\n        # for the middle full repetitions.\n        max_sum_two_arr = _find_max_subarray_sum(arr + arr)\n        \n        # The result is the maximum of:\n        # 1. The best subarray sum within a single array (max_sum_single_arr).\n        # 2. The best subarray sum spanning potentially across repetitions,\n        #    calculated from two arrays and extended by (k-2) full array sums.\n        return max(max_sum_single_arr, max_sum_two_arr + (k - 2) * total_sum_arr)\n    else:\n        # If total sum is zero or negative, repeating the array more than twice\n        # will not yield a larger sum than what's found in two concatenations.\n        # The max sum will be found within arr + arr.\n        return _find_max_subarray_sum(arr + arr)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/388", "solution": "def highest_Power_of_2(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n.\n    This implementation uses bit shifting for efficiency.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    power = 1\n    while (power << 1) <= n:\n        power <<= 1\n    return power"}
