{"task_id": "Mbpp/311", "solution": "def set_left_most_unset_bit(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Sets the leftmost (most significant) unset bit in the given integer.\n    If all bits up to n.bit_length() - 1 are set, it sets the next higher bit.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Input must be a non-negative integer.\")\n\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    msb_idx = n.bit_length() - 1\n\n    for i in range(msb_idx, -1, -1):\n        if not (n & (1 << i)):\n            return n | (1 << i)\n\n    return n | (1 << (msb_idx + 1))"}
