{"task_id": "Mbpp/415", "solution": "def max_Product(numbers: list[int]) -> tuple[int, int]:\n    # Sort the array to identify the two largest and two smallest numbers efficiently.\n    # This approach correctly handles cases involving negative numbers, where two small negatives can yield the highest product.\n    sorted_numbers = sorted(numbers)\n    n = len(sorted_numbers)\n\n    # Consider the product of the two largest numbers.\n    product_largest_pair = sorted_numbers[n-1] * sorted_numbers[n-2]\n    pair_largest = (sorted_numbers[n-2], sorted_numbers[n-1])\n\n    # Consider the product of the two smallest (most negative) numbers.\n    product_smallest_pair = sorted_numbers[0] * sorted_numbers[1]\n    pair_smallest = (sorted_numbers[0], sorted_numbers[1])\n\n    if product_largest_pair >= product_smallest_pair:\n        return pair_largest\n    else:\n        return pair_smallest"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/419", "solution": "from typing import Union\n\ndef round_and_sum(numbers: list[Union[float, int]]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Rounds every number in the list, sums them, and multiplies by the list's length.\n    This function processes a list of numbers to compute a final integer value.\n    \"\"\"\n    rounded_numbers = [round(num) for num in numbers]\n    total_sum = sum(rounded_numbers)\n    result = total_sum * len(numbers)\n    return result"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/422", "solution": "def find_Average_Of_Cube(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the average of the cubes of the first n natural numbers.\n    Uses the formula: ((n * (n + 1) / 2)^2) / n.\n    \"\"\"\n    sum_of_natural_numbers = n * (n + 1) // 2\n    sum_of_cubes = sum_of_natural_numbers ** 2\n    average = float(sum_of_cubes) / n\n    return average"}
