{"task_id": "Mbpp/445", "solution": "```python\nfrom typing import Tuple\n\ndef index_multiplication(\n    tuple1: Tuple[Tuple[int, int], ...],\n    tuple2: Tuple[Tuple[int, int], ...]\n) -> Tuple[Tuple[int, int], ...]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs index-wise multiplication of tuple elements in two given tuples.\n    Raises ValueError if input tuples have different lengths or if any inner\n    tuple is not of length 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(tuple1) != len(tuple2):\n        raise ValueError(\"Input tuples must have the same length.\")\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(tuple1)):\n        inner_tuple1 = tuple1[i]\n        inner_tuple2 = tuple2[i]\n\n        if len(inner_tuple1) != 2 or len(inner_tuple2) != 2:\n            raise ValueError(\"Inner tuples must be of length 2.\")\n\n        multiplied_inner_tuple = (\n            inner_tuple1[0] * inner_tuple2[0],\n            inner_tuple1[1] * inner_tuple2[1]\n        )\n        result.append(multiplied_inner_tuple)\n\n    return tuple(result)\n```"}
