{"task_id": "Mbpp/468", "solution": "def max_product(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    n = len(arr)\n    if n == 0:\n        return 0\n    if n == 1:\n        return arr[0]\n\n    # dp[i] stores the maximum product of an increasing subsequence ending at index i\n    dp = [0] * n\n\n    # Initialize dp array. Each element itself is an increasing subsequence of length 1.\n    for i in range(n):\n        dp[i] = arr[i]\n\n    # Initialize max_overall_product with the largest single element to handle all negative numbers correctly.\n    max_overall_product = max(arr)\n\n    for i in range(n):\n        for j in range(i):\n            # If arr[i] can extend an increasing subsequence ending at j\n            if arr[i] > arr[j]:\n                # Only extend if the previous product (dp[j]) is positive.\n                # Multiplying a positive arr[i] by a non-positive dp[j] would yield a non-positive or smaller product.\n                if dp[j] > 0:\n                    dp[i] = max(dp[i], dp[j] * arr[i])\n        # Update the overall maximum product found so far\n        max_overall_product = max(max_overall_product, dp[i])\n\n    return max_overall_product"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/473", "solution": "from typing import Any, List, Set, Tuple\n\ndef tuple_intersection(list1: List[Tuple[Any, ...]], list2: List[Tuple[Any, ...]]) -> Set[Tuple[Any, ...]]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the tuple intersection of elements in the given tuple lists, irrespective of their order.\n    The returned tuples will be in their original form as found in list1 if a match exists.\n    \"\"\"\n    def _normalize_tuple(t: Tuple[Any, ...]) -> Tuple[Any, ...]:\n        \"\"\"Converts a given tuple into a canonical form by sorting its elements for order-agnostic comparison.\"\"\"\n        return tuple(sorted(t))\n\n    normalized_to_original_map_1 = {}\n    for original_tuple in list1:\n        normalized_tuple = _normalize_tuple(original_tuple)\n        if normalized_tuple not in normalized_to_original_map_1:\n            normalized_to_original_map_1[normalized_tuple] = original_tuple\n\n    normalized_set_2 = {_normalize_tuple(t) for t in list2}\n\n    intersection_normalized_tuples = set(normalized_to_original_map_1.keys()).intersection(normalized_set_2)\n\n    result_set = {normalized_to_original_map_1[n_tuple] for n_tuple in intersection_normalized_tuples}\n\n    return result_set"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/555", "solution": "def difference(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the difference between the sum of cubes of the first n natural numbers\n    and the sum of the first n natural numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Calculate the sum of the first n natural numbers\n    # Formula: n * (n + 1) / 2\n    sum_natural_numbers = n * (n + 1) // 2\n\n    # Calculate the sum of the cubes of the first n natural numbers\n    # Formula: (sum_of_natural_numbers)^2\n    sum_cubes_natural_numbers = sum_natural_numbers * sum_natural_numbers\n\n    # Return the difference\n    return sum_cubes_natural_numbers - sum_natural_numbers"}
