{"task_id": "Mbpp/559", "solution": "def max_sub_array_sum(arr: list[int], length: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the sum of the largest contiguous sublist using Kadane's algorithm.\n    The 'length' parameter is redundant in Python and is not used.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not arr:\n        return 0\n\n    max_so_far = arr[0]\n    current_max = arr[0]\n\n    for i in range(1, len(arr)):\n        current_max = max(arr[i], current_max + arr[i])\n        max_so_far = max(max_so_far, current_max)\n    \n    return max_so_far"}
