{"task_id": "Mbpp/564", "solution": "import collections\n\ndef count_Pairs(numbers: list[int], __expect: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts the number of possible unordered pairs where both elements are unequal.\n    The `__expect` parameter is ignored and is only present to match the problem stub.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(numbers)\n\n    # Total possible unordered pairs from n distinct positions\n    total_possible_pairs = n * (n - 1) // 2\n\n    if total_possible_pairs == 0:\n        return 0\n\n    # Count occurrences of each number\n    counts = collections.Counter(numbers)\n\n    # Calculate pairs where elements are equal\n    equal_pairs_count = 0\n    for count in counts.values():\n        if count > 1:\n            equal_pairs_count += count * (count - 1) // 2\n\n    return total_possible_pairs - equal_pairs_count"}
