{"task_id": "Mbpp/577", "solution": "def last_Digit_Factorial(n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the last digit of the factorial of a given non-negative integer n.\n    For n >= 5, the last digit of n! is always 0.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or n == 1:\n        return 1\n    elif n == 2:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 3:\n        return 6\n    elif n == 4:\n        return 4\n    else:  # For n >= 5, n! will always end in 0\n        return 0"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "def is_Sub_Array(main_list, sublist):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if 'sublist' is a contiguous sublist of 'main_list'.\n    An empty list is considered a sublist of any list.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not sublist:\n        return True\n\n    n = len(main_list)\n    m = len(sublist)\n\n    if m > n:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(n - m + 1):\n        if main_list[i:i + m] == sublist:\n            return True\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/578", "solution": "def interleave_lists(list1: list, list2: list, list3: list) -> list:\n    \"\"\"\n    Interleaves three lists of the same length into a single flat list.\n    Raises ValueError if input lists do not have the same length.\n    \"\"\"\n    len1 = len(list1)\n    len2 = len(list2)\n    len3 = len(list3)\n\n    if not (len1 == len2 == len3):\n        raise ValueError(\"Lists must be of the same length.\")\n\n    interleaved_list = []\n    for i in range(len1):\n        interleaved_list.append(list1[i])\n        interleaved_list.append(list2[i])\n        interleaved_list.append(list3[i])\n\n    return interleaved_list"}
