{"task_id": "Mbpp/589", "solution": "import math\n\ndef perfect_squares(start, end):\n    \"\"\"Finds all perfect squares within the inclusive range [start, end].\"\"\"\n    perfect_squares_list = []\n    \n    # Perfect squares are non-negative, so the search effectively starts from 0 if 'start' is negative.\n    # The range function correctly handles cases where search_start > end by yielding an empty sequence.\n    search_start = max(0, start) \n\n    for num in range(search_start, end + 1):\n        # Check if num is a perfect square using integer square root.\n        sqrt_val = math.isqrt(num)\n        if sqrt_val * sqrt_val == num:\n            perfect_squares_list.append(num)\n            \n    return perfect_squares_list"}
