{"task_id": "Mbpp/594", "solution": "def diff_even_odd(numbers):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the first even and first odd number in a list and returns their absolute difference.\n    Assumes the list will contain at least one even and one odd number.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_even = None\n    first_odd = None\n\n    for num in numbers:\n        if first_even is None and num % 2 == 0:\n            first_even = num\n        if first_odd is None and num % 2 != 0:\n            first_odd = num\n        \n        if first_even is not None and first_odd is not None:\n            break\n            \n    return abs(first_even - first_odd)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/592", "solution": "import math\n\ndef binomial_coefficient(n: int, k: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(n, k).\n    Relies on math.comb for efficient calculation.\n    \"\"\"\n    return math.comb(n, k)\n\ndef sum_Of_product(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of the product of consecutive binomial coefficients.\n    Specifically, sum(C(n, k) * C(n, k+1)) for k from 0 to n-1.\n    \"\"\"\n    total_sum = 0\n    for k in range(n):\n        term1 = binomial_coefficient(n, k)\n        term2 = binomial_coefficient(n, k + 1)\n        total_sum += (term1 * term2)\n    return total_sum"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/598", "solution": "def armstrong_number(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if the given number is an Armstrong number.\n    An Armstrong number equals the sum of its digits, each raised to the power of the number of digits.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 10:\n        return True\n\n    num_str = str(number)\n    num_digits = len(num_str)\n    sum_of_powers = 0\n\n    for digit_char in num_str:\n        digit = int(digit_char)\n        sum_of_powers += digit ** num_digits\n\n    return sum_of_powers == number"}
