{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list[int], list2: list[int], n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    Assumes lists are sorted and of size n.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Current index for list1\n    j = 0  # Current index for list2\n    m1 = -1 # Stores the (n)-th element\n    m2 = -1 # Stores the (n+1)-th element\n\n    # The loop iterates n+1 times to find the (n)-th and (n+1)-th elements\n    # (0-indexed: elements at index n-1 and n) of the combined sorted list.\n    for count in range(n + 1):\n        if i == n: # list1 is exhausted\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n        elif j == n: # list2 is exhausted\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] <= list2[j]:\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list1[i]\n            i += 1\n        else: # list2[j] is smaller\n            m1 = m2\n            m2 = list2[j]\n            j += 1\n    \n    # The median is the average of the n-th and (n+1)-th smallest elements.\n    return (m1 + m2) / 2.0"}
